rvn-w4a16 only; no LIL/cutlass behaviour change -- the sweep touched here runs
only inside prepare_moe_nvfp4_layer_for_marlin, which the marlin MoE runner
reaches and the flashinfer_cutlass launch (LIL) never does.

Patch 0052 released the loader-format swizzle placeholders with delattr. The
cutedsl branches of ModelOptNvFp4FusedMoEMethod read those two attributes
eagerly: as keyword arguments (modelopt_quant.py:2940-2941), as a getattr
DEFAULT argument (:2960-2965, so the getattr cannot protect them) and inside
a list literal (:2989-2995). An attribute that no longer exists therefore
turns a path this function never reaches into an AttributeError.

None is already the class's own "unused" marker for these two slots:
create_weights assigns None for them on the trtllm and marlin branches
(:2382, :2407), and 0053 made that skip construction-time. Assigning None
releases exactly what delattr released -- the placeholder Parameter is the
only reference -- so the memory behaviour of 0052/0053 is unchanged.

Regression: tests/rvn_ple/test_rvn_ple_moe_release.py::
test_marlin_repack_nulls_rather_than_deletes_the_swizzle_slots is red on the
preimage (the attributes are gone) and green with this patch.

--- a/python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/marlin_utils_fp4.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/marlin_utils_fp4.py
@@ -453,7 +453,14 @@
     # guards on hasattr.
     for stale in ("w13_blockscale_swizzled", "w2_blockscale_swizzled"):
         if getattr(layer, stale, None) is not None:
-            delattr(layer, stale)
+            # Assign None instead of delattr: the cutedsl branches read these
+            # through eagerly evaluated arguments -- keyword defaults at
+            # modelopt_quant.py:2940-2941 and :2960-2965, a list literal at
+            # :2989-2995 -- so a missing attribute would turn a path this
+            # function never reaches into an AttributeError, while None stays
+            # the class's own "unused" marker for these two slots
+            # (modelopt_quant.py:2382, :2407).
+            setattr(layer, stale, None)
 
     w13 = layer.w13_weight.data
     w2 = layer.w2_weight.data
